@*
    Task 11.1 — the ASP.NET Core replacement for this plugin's web.config
    <system.web.webPages.razor><pages> element (Requirement 4.4).

    Identical in shape to tasks 10.1/10.2's; only the plugin's own Models namespace differs. See
    src/Plugins/Nop.Plugin.DiscountRules.CustomerRoles/Views/_ViewImports.cshtml for the full
    reasoning. In brief: all 20 plugins ship a byte-identical web.config declaring
    pageBaseType="Nop.Web.Framework.ViewEngines.Razor.WebViewPage" (→ the @inherits below, which
    is what makes T("…") and an unqualified @model resolve) plus four System.Web <namespaces>
    (→ the @using directives; System.Web.Mvc.Ajax has no ASP.NET Core counterpart and is
    dropped). Deleting the web.config without adding this file produces one CS0246 per @model
    plus one CS0103 per T(...) call.

    It must sit at Views/ and inside the project file's Content/Link glob (Views\**\*.cshtml):
    Razor resolves _ViewImports by walking up from the view's own directory, and the directory it
    walks is the LINKED one — so this file compiles as
    /Plugins/ExternalAuth.Facebook/Views/_ViewImports.cshtml, the same directory as
    Configure.cshtml and PublicInfo.cshtml. Linking the two inconsistently would make the imports
    silently not apply, and the failure would look like a missing model type.
*@
@inherits Nop.Web.Framework.ViewEngines.Razor.WebViewPage<TModel>

@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Html
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Rendering
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Routing

@*
    Nop.Web.Framework carries HtmlExtensions (Html.NopLabelFor / NopEditorFor /
    OverrideStoreCheckboxFor), ViewCompatibilityExtensions and ChildActionExtensions (the
    @Html.Action bridge). One import covers all of them, which is why no view call site here
    needed a new @using.
*@
@using Nop.Core.Infrastructure
@using Nop.Web.Framework
@using Nop.Web.Framework.UI
@using Nop.Plugin.ExternalAuth.Facebook.Models

@*
    Tag helpers. 3.90 had none (they do not exist in MVC 5). Added for the same reason task 7.3
    added them to Nop.Web: the framework's form/validation tag helpers are the supported route to
    an anti-forgery token, and Html.BeginForm uses the same infrastructure.
*@
@addTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
